    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="0392" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg382"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/1293</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Australian Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Casey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 269/41</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-11">December 11,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to convey to you the
                    following message which I have received from the Australian Minister for
                    External Affairs: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I desire to express the Commonwealth Government’s profound appreciation
                            of the initiative[,] courage and patience displayed by the President of
                            the United States and the Secretary of State in their endeavour to
                            prevent war in the Pacific and in their objective of outlawing force as
                            the instrument of national policy.</p>
                        <p>For the time being the attempt to maintain Pacific peace on the basis of
                            law and justice has been checked by the sudden and treacherous attack of
                            the Japanese forces while diplomatic negotiations were actually
                            proceeding.</p>
                        <p>The Commonwealth Government is honoured to be associated with the United
                            States in resisting the aggressors until they are finally overthrown and
                            until the principles for which the President has so frequently declared
                            are established not only in the Pacific but everywhere in the
                                world.”<anchor n="70" xml:id="d415-f1"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. G. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Casey</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d415-f1" n="70" xml:id="d415-f1-content">
                <p>In a communication dated December 18 to the Australian Minister, the Secretary of
                    State requested that his “sincere thanks” be conveyed to Mr. Evatt for the
                    message of December 11.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
